# Working engine is the core

Do not relocate or rewrite `tools/hvx_sdk_host/`, `app/services/hvx_client.py`, `app/services/gates.py`, or the port-30000 NetSDK sequence.

Blueprint folders live **inside** `app/domain`, `app/application`, and `app/infrastructure` as wrappers. Do not create a parallel `smartpark/` tree or switch default cameras to ONVIF/RTSP.

- Default `adapter_id` is `hvx`; unknown ids fall back to HVX
- SQLite stays the live store; PostgreSQL is only `SMARTPARK_DATABASE_URL`
- `DIRECT` is the live connection mode; `EDGE_AGENT` is reserved
- Gate default remains `COMMISSIONING` (physical still allowed). SHADOW only dry-runs *automatic* opens
- Docs are filled when a feature lands; do not empty-stub the 33-file list

```python
# BAD — new connect path that skips the host
await onvif.identify(camera)

# GOOD — wrap the working client
await HVXCameraAdapter().connect(camera)  # calls HVXHostClient.connect
```
